UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Canva AI 2.0 is the conversational core of Canva's Magic Studio, introduced at Canva Create 2026: you describe a design in text or voice and it returns an editable layout, built on Canva's own Design Model. Canva Craft, Canva's first in-house image-generation model, launched inside Dream Lab on October 22, 2026.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'canva-ai' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Canva AI is the AI layer inside Canva, the browser-based design platform used for social posts, presentations, documents, and marketing assets. Rather than a single feature, it is a conversational assistant that sits on top of the whole editor. Canva AI 2.0, unveiled at Canva Create 2026, recast Canva as a conversational, agentic assistant that Canva positions as part of a broader 'Creative Operating System,' adding connectors, scheduling, web research, brand intelligence, Sheets AI, and Canva Code 2.0. It runs on the Canva Design Model and introduced Magic Layers, which splits an AI-generated poster back into separate, editable layers; Magic Layers is also available inside ChatGPT and Gemini.

Canva Research has shipped two new models in quick succession. Canva Craft, the company's first in-house image-generation model, launched October 22, 2026 inside Dream Lab for all Canva users globally. It uses a two-stage architecture, in which a planning model writes a composition plan and a rendering model draws it, producing images at up to 2K resolution across 30 or more aspect ratios with text rendering in 55 languages, built to work well with Magic Layers. Craft is also reachable through Canva's Public API, with MCP server access listed as coming soon; Canva says Craft debuted 4th on the DesignArena image-generation leaderboard, which it describes as making Canva Research the 2nd-ranked lab for image generation. About a week later, on October 29-30, 2026, Canva Research launched Canva Brush, a vision-language model built for editing existing designs rather than generating new ones, handling anything from a single text element to a whole deck. Brush writes and runs code to modify design elements, then checks its own output and iterates; Canva claims it is up to 69% faster on general design-editing tasks and 46% lower cost per edit than its previous design agent. Which plans or surfaces Brush is available on has not been publicly confirmed.

Magic Studio bundles the rest of the toolkit: Magic Design for templates, Dream Lab (now powered by Craft) for image generation, Magic Write for copy, Canva Sheets and Magic Charts for data-to-visualization plus Magic Insights, and Magic Switch, which does AI-driven layout redesign rather than simple resizing. The assistant keeps persistent memory and stays aware of your brand assets.

Canva's pricing page lists a Free plan at $0 with a limited AI allowance shared across its Standard, Premium, and Ultra AI tools. Paid plans are billed annually: Pro is US$120 per year for one person, and Business is US$210 per year per person; Enterprise is custom-priced. Canva also sells AI Pass, a monthly add-on for Pro and Business accounts that multiplies the monthly AI allowance. Canva localizes pricing by region, so these US dollar figures, taken from canva.com/pricing, may differ outside the US, and no monthly US-dollar price for Pro or Business has been separately confirmed.

The limits are worth knowing. The free plan's shared AI allowance is capped, though the exact number isn't published; generation quality still varies and often needs manual cleanup; the conversational assistant is best for common formats rather than highly bespoke design work; MCP access for Canva Craft is listed as coming soon rather than live today; and Canva Brush's rollout, including which plans can use it, has not yet been confirmed publicly. It suits solo creators, small marketing teams, social media managers, and non-designers who want good-looking, on-brand assets fast without learning a professional design tool.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'canva-ai' AND lang = 'en';

