 WHERE slug = 'higgsfield' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Higgsfield is an AI creative platform that bundles third-party video and image models, such as Kling, Seedance, Google Veo and Nano Banana, with its own tools for ads, social clips and AI influencers. The company says it has more than 40 million users and passed a $1 billion annualized revenue run rate in September 2026.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'higgsfield' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Higgsfield is a web-based creative platform for making AI video, images and audio in one workspace. Instead of relying on one model, it gives subscribers access to many third-party models, including Kling, Seedance, Google Veo, Wan, MiniMax Hailuo, Nano Banana, FLUX and GPT Image, alongside its own models and tools such as Soul image generation, DoP video, Cinema Studio, Ads Studio, AI Influencer and Genjutsu.

On September 24, 2026, Higgsfield said it had crossed a $1 billion annualized revenue run rate, about 18 months after launching its creative suite. The company calculates this as the latest four weeks of revenue multiplied by 13, so it is a projection of current pace, not revenue earned over a year, and it is not audited. Higgsfield reports more than 40 million users in 238 countries and territories, nearly 1 million paying subscribers and work for 390 Fortune 500 companies. It raised a $400 million Series B at a $5.4 billion valuation in August 2026, and extended that round in October 2026 with TCV and NVIDIA joining as investors, though the new amount and valuation were not disclosed.

The platform covers text-to-video, image-to-video, motion control, image generation and editing, face and character swap, product placement and ad templates. You pick a model for each job and pay in credits. In late October 2026, Higgsfield also launched Playable, which lets users turn a text idea, artwork or gameplay recording into browser-based mini-games and playable ads. Higgsfield also offers an API, an MCP server, a Canvas workspace and Supercomputer, and team workspaces with pooled credits, admin spend controls, priority processing and custom SSO.

Pricing in US dollars, per month: a Free plan with limited use; Starter at $19, the same price whether billed monthly or annually, with a fixed 270 credits; Plus at $47 billed annually or $59 billed monthly with 1,200 credits and access to all models and features; and Ultra at $99 billed annually or $129 billed monthly with 3,000 credits, plus larger credit options. Team plans start at $65 per seat per month for 2 to 15 seats with pooled credits. Plus and Ultra include 7-day unlimited windows on selected models such as Kling and Nano Banana. Credit costs vary widely: about 7 credits per 5 seconds of Kling at 720p versus about 60 credits per 5 seconds of Seedance at 1080p. Prices exclude VAT.

The credit system takes effort to budget, because cost depends on model, resolution and clip length. The unlimited offers are time-limited, apply only on higgsfield.ai (not via MCP, CLI, Canvas or Supercomputer) and can be slowed during high traffic. Starter only includes selected models. Most of the underlying models are made by other companies and can also be used directly, and the revenue and growth figures are the company's own unaudited claims.

Higgsfield suits marketers, agencies and creators who produce ads and social video at volume and want many leading models under one subscription, with ready-made workflows for product shots, AI presenters and now interactive mini-games and ads. If you only need one model, a direct subscription to Kling AI or Runway can be simpler.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'higgsfield' AND lang = 'en';

