UPDATE tools SET best_for = $x$AI image, video and audio generation across many leading third-party models, plus 250M+ stock assets$x$
 WHERE slug = 'freepik' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Magnific, the name Freepik has used since April 2026, is an AI creative platform that combines image, video and audio generation using many leading third-party models with a library of more than 250 million stock assets. Paid plans add credits, unlimited generation on selected models and a commercial license.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'freepik' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Freepik started in Málaga in 2010 as a search engine for free graphic resources and grew into one of the largest stock libraries for photos, vectors, icons and templates. On April 28, 2026 it rebranded as Magnific, the name of the AI upscaling startup it acquired in May 2024, to bring its stock library, generative AI tools and upscalers under one brand. freepik.com now redirects to magnific.com.

Magnific gives subscribers access to leading third-party models, including Kling, Seedance, Google Veo, Gemini Omni, MiniMax, Nano Banana, FLUX, Recraft, Ideogram and Grok for images and video, plus Google Lyria and ElevenLabs for music and sound effects. Its own Magnific One image model and a Brand Kit feature are now included in all paid plans.

Beyond generation, Magnific includes Spaces, a shared canvas for building workflows, pro editing tools for image, video and design, the Magnific image and video upscalers, music, voice and sound effect generation, custom AI characters on paid plans, an MCP server and plugins, a ComfyUI integration, API access and metadata export. The stock library of more than 250 million photos, videos, vectors and PSDs is part of the same subscription.

Individual plans on the Magnific pricing page are Premium, Premium+ (labeled 'Best value') and Pro Starter (labeled 'Expert choice'); separate Teams plans, including Business and Enterprise, are available for organizations under a different tab. Web prices are shown in local currency and are not published in US dollars; for example, pricing fetched from Israel shows Premium at roughly ₪59 a month or ₪40 a month on annual billing, Premium+ at about ₪132 or ₪99, and Pro Starter at about ₪322 or ₪241.50, all excluding VAT. In the US App Store, in-app subscription pricing lists Premium at $26.00 a month or $234.99 a year, and Premium+ at $55.00 a month or $494.99 a year; Pro Starter is not listed there. Credits are issued annually and do not reset monthly: Premium includes 240,000 credits a year, Premium+ includes 600,000 a year, and Pro Starter includes 1.5 million or 4 million a year depending on which image models are covered. Most paid plans include unlimited generation on select image models for part or all of the year, though the exact set of unlimited models can vary by plan.

There is no confirmed free plan on the current pricing page, and prices vary by region with frequent promotions, so there is no single published US dollar price list for the web. Credit costs vary widely: a Nano Banana image at 2K resolution uses 75 credits, while 4 seconds of Seedance video at 1080p uses 4,400 credits. Video, audio and editing tools still consume credits even on plans with unlimited image generation, and video is especially credit-intensive. The April 2026 rebrand means older Freepik links and guides now point to Magnific, which can cause some confusion.

Magnific suits designers, marketers and agencies who want stock content and many AI models in one subscription, especially for high volumes of images. If you only need one image model, Midjourney, Leonardo AI or Krea AI may be simpler, and Adobe Firefly fits teams already using Adobe Creative Cloud.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'freepik' AND lang = 'en';

